.TH RASKIN 1
.SH NAME
raskin \- Read macOS preferences into KDL and generate native commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraskin\fR [COMMAND]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Capture persisted macOS preferences as editable KDL, then generate a standalone .macos file. Raskin never executes generated commands. Capture is broad by default; desktop, input, and power select curated subsets.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-usage\-spec\fR
Emit the jdx/usage interface specification
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBcapture\fR
Read explicit persisted user, host, system and container preferences plus native power profiles. Unavailable settings are omitted from KDL; capture diagnostics go to stderr. No settings are changed. With \-\-from, only the supplied offline tree is read; there is no live fallback.
.TP
\fBgenerate\fR
Validate saved KDL and emit native commands for a human to inspect and run. Generation never reads host settings or executes commands. Unsupported values fail before any output unless \-\-skip\-unsupported explicitly requests a partial script.
.SH "RASKIN CAPTURE"
Read explicit persisted user, host, system and container preferences plus native power profiles. Unavailable settings are omitted from KDL; capture diagnostics go to stderr. No settings are changed. With \-\-from, only the supplied offline tree is read; there is no live fallback.
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR raskin capture [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fR
Show per\-source capture diagnostics on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-preset\fR \fI<PRESET>\fR
Capture broad settings or a curated subset
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRbroad
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<DIRECTORY>\fR
Read an offline tree containing user/, system/, containers/, host\-id.txt, and pmset.txt
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write KDL to this path; otherwise use stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Atomically replace an existing output file
.SH "RASKIN GENERATE"
Validate saved KDL and emit native commands for a human to inspect and run. Generation never reads host settings or executes commands. Unsupported values fail before any output unless \-\-skip\-unsupported explicitly requests a partial script.
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR raskin generate [OPTIONS] <INPUT>
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fR
Show per\-setting generation diagnostics on stderr
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write the script to this path; otherwise use stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Atomically replace an existing output file
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-unsupported\fR
Omit unsupported settings, naming each in script comments; use \-\-verbose for details on stderr
\fBArguments:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB<INPUT>\fR
KDL input path, or \- to read stdin
